rigorous treatment as any other field of science. It seems when respected
scientists publish wild speculations they are treated with kid gloves and that
should not be the case.

(I include Penrose for his assertion that the brain works by exploiting
effects in the vapor-theory of quantum gravity. Wheeler for his participatory
anthoropical principle. Josephson for his crackpot speculations of why
how paranormal phenomena work. [EPR effects, fifth forces of nature, etc]
