  Nick Szabo talks about frying food and carcinogens. I can only say that the
link between fried food and cancer has not been established. A couple of
years ago, I read an article in science news that put this carcinogen/mutagen
paranoia to rest.  Basically, a scientist analyzed a cross section of human
foods (fruits, vegetables, meats, well-water, cooked foods) and found
that each contained a few hundred mutagenic chemicals that, if consumed in
enough quantity over life, would cause cancer in humans.  Even breathing
oxygen has the potential to cause cancer. The risk to your life was about
a few days shaved off your lifespan.

  You're more likely to die because of bacteria in uncooked foods than you
are of carcinogens in cooked foods. The concern over hot foods in the
esophogus seems to be even more paranoid.  If you're concerned over a risk
like that, you better not leave your house or let sunlight in.

  Nick told me privately that I better have my life insurance paid up because
I eat foods that have been broiled/fried (e.g. chicken/steak/etc) I find
this a paranoid view. Such food isn't likely to cause cancer until your
in your 80s. That's 60 years away for me, 60 years of biotech/medical
development. I'm much rather take steps to reduce more important risks
in my life, such as heart disease, diabetes, and death on the highway.
In my family treat dating back a hundred years, nobody in my family
died of cancer. Heart disease and diabetes killed most people in my
family in their 60s/70s.

  Nick, do you also fear the VLF/ELF radiation from electric components in 
your house.

  

