From: Andrew S Hall <ashall@magnus.acs.ohio-state.edu>
Subject: DIET: Vegan, etc

Before anyone makes a total dietary switch to vegan for the sake of life
extensions, there is a couple things to consider.

There are some really interesting studies being done on why the French
appear to have longer life spans despite their atrocious (but delish) diet.
I think there is a book called _The Paradox of the French_ about this.
One group has attributed this to a particular component (not yet totally 
isolated) in red wine. If such chemicals that counter the harmful effects
of an unhealthy diet exist, there may be no reason to change the diet.
Better living thru science!

I am unconvinced of these results, though. My personal theory is that the
lack of strong chemical presvatives in the diet is the deciding factors. If a 
chemical is strong enough to prevent natural degradation of proteins and 
carbohydrates, then it seems likely it would have an effect in the body.
It could possibily contribute to longer lifespans of harmful compounds rather 
than let the body natural break them down. I know of no studies on this and
have only my experience in molecular biology to back me up.

There is an irony in some extropians using studies in cancer causation and 
other "evidence" to back up their claim that Vegan is a life-extending diet.
(I don't say this to insult anyone, either.) The methodology of many studies
in cancer (and other illnesses) etiology as related to diet is as weak as the
methodology (and often the same) as people have criticized the FDA for relying
on in its rulings. There are two methods. One is the our little furry friends 
and mega-dosing. The other is statistical correlation. Both of these are used 
in both drug/product testing AND in cnacer/illness etiology.

Personally, I love meat and it would take a solid study to convince me. I pride
myself on being a very good cook and think if Ray ever came by, I could whip
up something he would love. Desert is usually the toughest, but *nobody* has
disliked my strawberry-banana frozen tofu pie. :)

